  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "epi_c",
      "defType": "meta/comment",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": -384
      },
      "params": {
        "text": "Epidemic (SIR)\n\n320 people wander a square; each is susceptible (blue), infected (red) or recovered (grey). Every frame each person finds the nearest infected one (Lookup's `nearest` op) and, if they're closer than the infection radius, catches it with a chance per second. The sick recover after a while; with waning immunity the recovered slowly become susceptible again, and the outbreak comes back in waves. Positions, states and sick-times are Read* / Write* state; the chart keeps the last 40 s of counts.\n\n• Click or drag in the square: infect the people under the cursor.\n• Sliders: `radius` (contagion distance), `speed` (how far people roam), `recover` (seconds sick), `waning` (immunity lost per second).\n• Toggle: lockdown (everyone slows to a crawl).\n• Presets panel: Flu, Measles, Endemic.",
        "width": 560,
        "height": 320
      },
      "portValues": {
        "text": "Epidemic (SIR)\n\n320 people wander a square; each is susceptible (blue), infected (red) or recovered (grey). Every frame each person finds the nearest infected one (Lookup's `nearest` op) and, if they're closer than the infection radius, catches it with a chance per second. The sick recover after a while; with waning immunity the recovered slowly become susceptible again, and the outbreak comes back in waves. Positions, states and sick-times are Read* / Write* state; the chart keeps the last 40 s of counts.\n\n• Click or drag in the square: infect the people under the cursor.\n• Sliders: `radius` (contagion distance), `speed` (how far people roam), `recover` (seconds sick), `waning` (immunity lost per second).\n• Toggle: lockdown (everyone slows to a crawl).\n• Presets panel: Flu, Measles, Endemic.",
        "width": 560,
        "height": 320
      }
    },
